[32m+[m[32m        f" parent's source and pass against their own — the test byte-identical in both trees, so nothing but the"[m
[32m+[m[32m        f" commit moved. On {unbuildable} more the parent tree cannot load the test at all, which is a harder"[m
[32m+[m[32m        f" differential than a failing assertion rather than a softer one. <strong>{green}</strong> pass on both"[m
[32m+[m[32m        " arms, which is what a commit that only adds a test, or duplicates a fix already on main, is supposed to"[m
[32m+[m[32m        " do. The rest of the branch is"[m
